  (b) DE12's mechanism is absent from H_Y: the WKB count of the full action finds no k^0 term except the gas's own pressure (B1: PASS), and DE12's convention (k = 1/kpc, 1e6 K) gives zero growth on all 24 hosts (B2: PASS).
      H_Y's yield surfaces carry a divergent longitudinal susceptibility, Q'' = dx/dy ~ (y - y_th)^(-1/2): it enters the baryons'
      k^-2 (Jeans) term; gas growth stays bounded and converged (B3: PASS; max 31.2 H); cold matter grows faster the finer it is resolved, Gamma ~ d_min^(-1/4), up to the xi filter: the isolated surface mode has p = 0.238-0.250 and reaches 204-451 H at xi (B4b: PASS);
      B4 as declared (FAIL) fitted the whole domain's maximum, which at z >= 2.5 and d_min >= 1 kpc is an interior dense-gas mode (p down to 0.045).
